From: damnbitimcrit <333091414+damnbitimcrit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Halo 3] Keep the effect state of Theater rewind snapshots

While a multiplayer film plays in Theater, every 300 ticks the game
copies its state into a rewind cache (cache1:\sf_history.blob, 16 slots)
and a seek back restores the nearest one. The GPU effect storages in it
were stale, so effects alive then glitched after seeking back; reading
them back at the snapshot would pause playback every 10 seconds.

halo3_gpu_readback_film_snapshots (default on, with halo3_gpu_readback)
uses the guest snapshots instead (halo3_theater.cc):
- 820A4580, after the snapshot's before-save procs (render thread
  parked, fence after the last effect pass waited; r30 = the slot):
  post the four effect storage windows for the slot.
- 820A4650: if writing the record failed (r28 = 0), the game still
  commits the slot over the previous record, so drop what was posted.
- 821D698C, in the before-load procs of every game state load, after
  their fence wait: flush, so no copy sees loaded data.
- 8227FB34, restoring a slot after the image read into B passed its
  marker or hash check, before sub_821E1C98 (8227FB44, which makes the
  clip's start state when a clip starts there) and the sample CRC:
  if the image carries the snapshot marker, take the slot's bytes
  (waiting only if the copy isn't done) and write them into B through
  the physical view, never over the CRC words or the hash field, then
  invalidate the GPU copy of those pages.

All four are reached only as described (fall-through, or the three
failure branches for 820A4650).

The main thread spends tens of microseconds per snapshot. One info line
per restore of a snapshot taken during playback, with what was put back
and counters since the previous such line.
